{
	quest.07791540478B3E02.quest_desc: ["&eWheel Modules&r are like &eLever Modules&r, but instead of going forward and backwards they only go left and right. \\n\\n&eWheel Modules&r will send &cRedstone Signals&r to what is set to the left or right to whatever &cFrequencies&r you have set. \\n\\nThe default is where you move your Mouse, but that can be changed. \\n\\n&eWheel Modules&r are Large Modules so you can only place 1. These can have &eButton Modules&r placed on top of them. Perfect for a Horn!"]
	quest.07791540478B3E02.title: "&eWheel Module"
	quest.0888AD88724FD90E.quest_desc: ["The &eJoystick&r is like an upgrade to the &eLever Module&r. \\n\\n&eLevers&r go forwards and backwards, but &eJoysticks&r go forwards, backwards, left, and right! \\n\\nEach of these directions can be set to a &cFrequency&r and the number it is set to, determines the strength of &cRedstone Signal&r sent out. \\n\\nThe default keybinds for the &eJoystick&r is the direction you move your Mouse, but that can be changed. They also keep the &cSignal&r until you change it like &eLevers&r do. \\n\\nThese are also Small Modules so they can be placed in Small or Large Module areas. Plus you can toss a &eButton Module&r on top of the &eJoystick&r."]
	quest.0888AD88724FD90E.title: "&eJoystick Module"
	quest.0BB2E4272797DB5D.quest_desc: ["&b&lAeronautics&r, just like &6&lCreate&r, comes with its own &b&lAddons&r! \\n\\nAddons of an Addon. \\n\\nHere you can find a whole bunch of Items and Blocks from these &b&lAddons&r to help upgrade your &bContraptions&r!"]
	quest.0BB2E4272797DB5D.title: "&b&lAeronautic Addons"
	quest.0D90241FB7B304ED.quest_desc: ["The &aVector Bearing&r can be set to attach a Block (or group of &aGlued&r Blocks) to the &aBearing&r in order to move them when the &aBearing&r is given &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nJust place the Block or Blocks down to the &aBearing&r, Right Click the top of the &aBearing&r to set it, and give it &dRotational Power&r to move it all. \\n\\nThe &aVector Bearing&r will also tilt toward certain Sides if there's a &cRedstone Signal&r on that side. A &cRedstone Signal&r on the North side with make it face the &aBearing&r North. The higher the Strength the farther it tilts. You can use them from multiple sides as well to tilt it at a diagonal. \\n\\nIf you Shift Right Click the &aBearing&r you can open its GUI. Here you can set &cRedstone Frequencies&r to each side it tilts to make it wireless. Or change how it responds. Or even how far it can tilt!"]
	quest.0D90241FB7B304ED.title: "&aVector Bearing"
	quest.10911940A0FADBAF.quest_desc: ["&eButton Keypads&r work exactly like &eButton Panels&r, just with 9 &eButtons&r instead of 4. \\n\\nAlso a Large Module."]
	quest.10911940A0FADBAF.title: "&eButton Keypad Module"
	quest.1496D098BB50CA3A.quest_desc: ["&eButton Panels&r are a group of 4 &eButtons&r. \\n\\nEach one of them can be set to a certain Keybind and &cFrequency&r. \\n\\nThey only fit in the Large Module area."]
	quest.1496D098BB50CA3A.title: "&eButton Panel Module"
	quest.1FB0AB389DB2EC19.quest_desc: ["We can boost our &bThrusters&r with 2 different Upgrades. \\n\\n&5Propulsion Upgrades&r go into the &bThrusters&r themselves and will upgrade the &bThrust&r they generate. \\n\\nThe better the &5Upgrade&r the more &bThrust&r, but also more Fuel consumption. \\n\\nOr we can upgrade the &cFuel&r by processing it through a &cFuel Oxidizer&r. Fluid goes in one hole, out the other. With &dRotational Power&r given to it via the &dCog&r, it will Oxidize the &cFuel&r."]
	quest.1FB0AB389DB2EC19.title: "&bThruster&r Boosts"
	quest.2090D6B29F48D121.quest_desc: ["&aAileron Bearings&r take two &aBearings&r and attach them together, sandwich wise! \\n\\nIt has a &3Blue face&r and an &6Orange face&r. Each can be attached to a Block or group of &aGlued&r Blocks by Right Clicking the top of the face. \\n\\nThe &aAileron&r has different modes it uses which we can toggle. By default it uses Single which will only move the &3Blue face&r when given &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nYou can also use Mirrored which moves both faces to the same degree in the same direction. Opposed which moves them to the same degree but opposite direction. \\n\\nYou can Shift Right Click to open its GUI to set &cRedstone Frequencies&r and max angles for each side."]
	quest.2090D6B29F48D121.title: "&aAileron Bearing"
	quest.20E49977F13CF87E.quest_desc: ["&l&7Create Propulsion&r brings its &aEnergy&r via &aCables&r. Just &aCables&r. \\n\\n&aCables&r will connect any Blocks that take or give &aEnergy&r and move it. They don't have Push or Pull sides, everything just moves freely. \\n\\nThey also have one &aGenerator&r to make &aEnergy&r, the &aCoral Generator&r. \\n\\n&cCoral&r as in the Fluid, not Sea Coral. This &cCoral&r is made by Mixing &cRedstone&f, &6Blaze Powder&f, and a &cPotion of Healing&r in a Super Heated Basin. \\n\\n&cCoral&r can be Piped in from the sides while &aEnergy&r goes out the top and bottom."]
	quest.20E49977F13CF87E.title: "&aEnergy &rfrom &l&7Create Propulsion"
	quest.2167EE6E4D86025F.quest_desc: ["&cBalloons&r are fun Items we can attach to &bPhysics Contraptions&r. \\n\\nThe &bContraption&r needs to be Assembled to place down a &cBalloon&r. \\n\\nOnce placed, it will generate Lift. Not much, but don't worry; more Blocks means more &cBalloons&r! \\n\\nYou can Left Click to break all the &cBalloons&r, or use a &6Wrench&r to only take down one. \\n\\nIf the &bContraption&r Disassembles, the &cBalloons&r will snap to the nearest &bAssembled Contraption&r."]
	quest.2167EE6E4D86025F.title: "&cRed &fBalloon"
	quest.2C2404FE2ABC0E3F.quest_desc: ["Hate using dirty old Fossile Fuels and... Lava? Why not use the &aThruster Lens&r! \\n\\nWhen you put a &aThruster Lens&r into the &bThruster&r, it will change it from using Fuel to make Smoke, to using &aForge Energy&r to make Lasers. \\n\\nLasers are healthier for the planet! \\n\\nIt also replaces the Plume Scroll with a Scroll for the Lasers Opacity. You can set it to 0 to get rid of the Laser entirely."]
	quest.2C2404FE2ABC0E3F.title: "Laser &bThuster&r?"
	quest.2EABFC803AD33209.quest_desc: ["&bSolid Fuel Thrusters&r work similar to &bFluid Thrusters&r in a few ways. \\n\\nBoth generate &bThrust&r in the direction they're facing and can have their Fuel automatically Piped in from behind. \\n\\n&bSolid Fuel Thrusters&r don't use the &cRedstone Signal&r to determine &bThrust&r, only to turn it on or off. \\n\\n&bSolid Fuel Thrusters&r also don't use &cLava &for &6Turpentine&r, they use &cFurnace Fuels &fand &cBlaze Cakes&r. \\n\\nThey also don't combine into 2x2x2 &bThrusters&r or 3x3x3."]
	quest.2EABFC803AD33209.title: "&bSolid Fuel Thruster"
	quest.31ED86EEAB66488A.quest_desc: ["&6Powered Ziplines&r connect to &6Ropes&r hanging between &6Connectors &for &6Winches&r. \\n\\nThey come with a Handle on the bottom you can hang from by Right Clicking (Shift to get off), and you can Place Blocks on top of them which will automatically be &aGlued&r to the &6Zipline&r. \\n\\nBy default they move with W and S, but with Shift Right Clicking the &6Zipline&r you can set &cRedstone Frequencies&r to it."]
	quest.31ED86EEAB66488A.title: "&6Powered Zipline"
	quest.32AFE9387E934DF1.quest_desc: ["&bGyroscopes&r are big wheels that Spin to try and keep everything stable. \\n\\nWhen used in &bPhysics Contraptions&r and given &dRotational Power&r, they'll generate whatever force is needed to help keep things balanced. \\n\\nBe careful though, too much Speed for the &bGyroscope&r can hurt more than help!"]
	quest.32AFE9387E934DF1.title: "&bGyroscope"
	quest.32C98CCAC1031D5B.quest_desc: ["Why care about using any Fuel for our &bThrusters&r when we can just power them with &aEnergy&r! \\n\\n&aIon Thrusters&r will take &aFE &fand &cRedstone&r to generate &bThrust&r. \\n\\nLike &bFluid Thrusters&r their &bThrust&r is determined by the strength of the &cRedstone Signal&r. \\n\\nThey also can't combine into 2x2x2 or 3x3x3 &bThrusters&r."]
	quest.32C98CCAC1031D5B.title: "&aIon Thruster"
	quest.3459AFA6C7E5C282.quest_desc: ["These &bThrusters&r (from &l&7Create Propulsion&r) are &bLiquid Thrusters&r. \\n\\nThey use &cLiquid Fuel&r which can be Piped in from the back of the &bThruster &fand a &cRedstone Signal&r which starts the &bThruster&r and determines the Force of the &bThrust&r. \\n\\nYou can also combine &bThrusters&r together in a 2x2x2 or 3x3x3 area to make one large or one even larger &bThruster&r. \\n\\nWith both the 2x2x2 and 3x3x3 &bThruster&r, you'll need to Pipe in Fuel from the back of the &bThrusters&r. \\n\\n&cLava&r and &6Turpentine&r are 2 Liquid Fuels you can use. There's probably others... &bOxidizer&r and &cCoral&r aren't them though."]
	quest.3459AFA6C7E5C282.title: "&bLiquid Fuel Thruster"
	quest.347CEFCF015F5C4F.quest_desc: ["&l&6Create Gadgets and Gizmos&r comes with its own introduction into &aEnergy&r. \\n\\nHere we have &aAndesite Cables&r which can transport &aFE&r. Similar to other &aEnergy Pipes&r. Except they don't interact with Wrenches, either they connect or they don't. \\n\\nWe also have the &aAlternator&r which will turn &dRotational Power&r into &aEnergy&r and the &dMotor&r which will turn &aEnergy&r into &dRotational Power&r."]
	quest.347CEFCF015F5C4F.title: "&aEnergy&r from &l&6Create Gadgets and Gizmos"
	quest.36A5A92AAD9DAC7A.quest_desc: ["&dStirling Generators&r use &cBurners&r beneath them to generate &dRotational Power&r. Perfect for on the move &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nIf you have a &cSolid Burner&r it will burn Furnace Fuels and &cBlaze Cakes&r. \\n\\n&cFluid Burners&r will use &cLava&r and Turpentine. \\n\\nYou can toggle the Speed and Direction of the &dGenerator&r on the top of it."]
	quest.36A5A92AAD9DAC7A.title: "Another &dRotational Power&r Generator"
	quest.3C5E6C2EDE96FB6A.quest_desc: ["&7Wings &fand &7Tempered Wings&r act just like &eSails&r for &bPhysics Contraptions&r. \\n\\nThere's currently no difference from normal and &7Tempered&r, maybe some day there will be. "]
	quest.3C5E6C2EDE96FB6A.title: "&7Wings"
	quest.3C6C35D6E4BB67C0.quest_desc: ["&eYokes&r are &eJoysticks&r specifically made for Aircrafts. \\n\\nIn real life it moves like a Steering Wheel to turn, but also comes forward and backwards to move the Plane to ascend or descend. \\n\\nHere it works just like the &eJoystick&r, but being a Large Module. \\n\\n&eYokes&r can also hold 2 &eButton Modules&r on them, unlike the &eJoystick's&r 1 &eButton&r."]
	quest.3C6C35D6E4BB67C0.title: "&eYoke Module"
	quest.3CBC2DB7685F45D2.quest_desc: ["&7Copycat Wings&r act like both &7Wings&r and &eSails&r, just we can add any Block in them to change how they look like a Framed Block!"]
	quest.3CBC2DB7685F45D2.title: "&7Copycat Wing"
	quest.3DB0DD9D94C9A892.quest_desc: ["&bVector Thruster&r and &bFluid Vector Thrusters&r are &bThrusters&r that we can use &cRedstone Signals&r with to aim! \\n\\n&bVector Thrusters&r take &aEnergy&r while &bFluid Vector Thrusters&r still take &cFluid Fuels&r from behind. \\n\\nBoth will use a &cRedstone Signal&r to start blasting away, with the &cSignal&r determining how much &bThrust&r is generated. \\n\\nTo aim the &bThrusters&r, you'll need to set &cRedstone Frequencies&r on each side of the &bThruster&r. \\n\\nThe higher&c Signal&r, the farther in that direction it will aim. You can use multiple at a time to aim in diagonals!"]
	quest.3DB0DD9D94C9A892.title: "&bVector Thrusters"
	quest.3DE2F153C7CFF07E.quest_desc: ["&eButton Modules&r are somehow the simplest and most complicated &eModules&r. \\n\\nYou can place 1 or 2 &eButton Modules&r on a &cDesk&r. By default they use Left Click, but you can change it and its &cFrequency&r. \\n\\nEverytime you Press and Hold the &eButton&r, a &cRedstone Signal&r will be sent out at full Strength. Once you let go, the &cSignal&r will end. \\n\\n&eButton Modules&r can also be placed on top of other &eModules&r!"]
	quest.3DE2F153C7CFF07E.title: "&eButton Module"
	quest.3FC6FAF3D86989E3.quest_desc: ["&dSmart Gearboxs&r work in a unique way to transport 2 different &8Shafts&r through the same Block. \\n\\nThere's 2 &8Shafts&r in one &dGearbox&r, each moving their own way. &dRotational Power&r given to the North side will only come out of the South side. Same with one given to the East side will only come out of the West side. \\n\\nYou can also Right Click the side to switch the direction of &dRotational Power&r with ease. \\n\\nThere's a Toggle on the top side of the &dSmart Gearbox&r which can change it to Locked or Passthrough Split. \\n\\nLocked will stop passing &dRotational Power&r through at all. While Passthrough Split will take &dRotational Power&r from one side and give it out to the other 3."]
	quest.3FC6FAF3D86989E3.title: "&dSmart Gearbox"
	quest.450AAB65EEDF267D.quest_desc: ["These Machines all work with &6Rope&r. \\n\\nWe went through how &6Rope&r works in the &b&lAeronautics&r chapter itself."]
	quest.450AAB65EEDF267D.title: "More &6Rope&r!"
	quest.46786A0A60689189.quest_desc: ["&dStepper Servos&r work similar to &dMechanical&r ones, they'll take in &dRotation Power&r and &cRedstone Signal&r and give out a specific Degree. \\n\\nThe &dStepper&r instead of working with start and end angles, uses Step Sizes. Step Sizes are what will multiply by the &cRedstone Signal&r to get our angle. \\n\\n2 Step with a 4 Strength &cRedstone Signal&r will set the angle to 8 degrees. 16 Step with 2 Strength &cRedstone Signal&r will set it to 32 degrees. \\n\\nThe &dStepper&r decides which way to turn to the set angle by where the &cRedstone Signal&r comes from. If it comes with both sides though, it will hold the angle in place until one or both &cSignals&r end."]
	quest.46786A0A60689189.title: "&dStepper Servo"
	quest.477D39CCFBD15873.quest_desc: [
		"&bThrusters&r (from &l&6Create Gadgets and Gizmos&r) use Fuel and a &cRedstone Signal&r to generate &bThrust&r. \\n\\nSimilar to Burners, but in any direction! \\nYou can use Fluid Fuels like &cLava&r which will need to be Piped in, or &bBlaze Burner Fuels&r which can be tossed into it. \\n\\nOur &bThrusters&r will then need the &cRedstone Signal&r. The strength given to it will determine how much &bThrust&r it gives. Full &cSignal&r, full &bThrust&r. \\n\\nBy Shift Right Clicking you can open its GUI which gives us a lot more options we'll talk about in the next page!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Here we get all the toggles we can dream of! \\n\\nYou can Scroll to set the Minimum or Maximum &bThrust&r. Minimum is when it will activate when it reaches a certain &bThrust&r while Maximum is when it won't generate any more &bThrust&r. \\n\\nNext Scroll effects Plume... not sure what that does but it doesn't seem too important! \\n\\nThen, with the Buttons we can change what turns the &bThruster&r on or off. &cRedstone&r, Computers, or just all on its own. \\n\\nNext 3 Slots are for Items that change the &bThruster&r, we'll talk about each of those individually. \\n\\nLast is our Fuel Slot and Bar. Slot for Item Fuel, Bar for Fluid Fuel."
	]
	quest.477D39CCFBD15873.quest_subtitle: "Gadgets and Gizmos"
	quest.477D39CCFBD15873.title: "&bThruster"
	quest.4B2DD219B7D5C1F8.quest_desc: ["&cControl Desks/Stands&r are used for an even greater control over &cRedstone Signals&r. \\n\\n&cDesks/Stands&r need &eModules&r Attached to them. Each has a certain amount that can be attached to each &cDesk/Stand&r. If you need more space just place down more &cDesk/Stands&r next to the other ones. \\n\\nTo place down &eModules&r just Right Click them onto the &cDesk/Stand&r. You'll need a &6Wrench&r to take them out. \\n\\nShift Right Clicking the &cDesk/Stand&r will bring up the configs. Here you can set &eModules&r to functions and &cFrequencies&r. \\n\\nThen, normal Right Clicking will allow you to use the &cStand/Desk&r. Here all inputs just go to whatever is set. Besides ESC, that's how you stop using the &cDesk/Stand&r."]
	quest.4B2DD219B7D5C1F8.title: "&cControl Desk/Stand"
	quest.52A207BF6F7076DD.quest_desc: ["&cTilt Adapters&r take &dRotational Power&r from below and &cRedstone Signals&r from the sides in order to send a direct angle on top. \\n\\nThe Strength at each side determines the angle it is set to. \\n\\nThe Advanced version gives us a set max angle for each side that we can toggle from 0 to 90."]
	quest.52A207BF6F7076DD.title: "&cTilt Adapters"
	quest.5365590B7227BD68.quest_desc: ["The &6Claw&r can grab onto &6Rope Connectors&r that are a part of &bPhysics Contraptions&r. \\n\\n&6Claws&r attach to &6Rope Winches&r, you'll need &6Rope&r to combine them. When the &6Winch&r lets down &6Rope&r, the &6Claw&r will lower. If it takes &6Rope&r back, it'll bring the &6Claw&r up. \\n\\nThe &6Claw&r can grab and drop &bContraptions&r with you Right Clicking it or controlling it with &cRedstone&r. \\n\\nShift Right Click to set its &cFrequency&r, then when it recieves a &cSignal&r it will hold. Once the &cSignal&r ends it will drop. \\n\\nThe &6Connector&r and &6Claw&r need to be leveled with each other for the &6Claw&r to pick it up."]
	quest.5365590B7227BD68.quest_subtitle: "I have been chosen, farewell my friends!"
	quest.5365590B7227BD68.title: "&6Claw"
	quest.5970C3B882D07A26.quest_desc: ["The &eThrottle Quandrant&r gives us 4 &eLevers&r in one Large Module. \\n\\nAll of them move forwards and backwards and will give a &cRedstone Signal&r based on the number it is at. \\n\\nThey do not come with default Keys so if you want any of them working you'll need to set their Keybinds and &cFrequencies&r. \\n\\nIf you don't want to use all 4 &eThrottles&r, you don't have to! Just only set as many as you need and leave the rest empty."]
	quest.5970C3B882D07A26.title: "&eThrottle Module"
	quest.5AC445CBF7B3744D.quest_desc: ["Physics Goggles do all the same as Avaitor's Goggles, plus more! \\n\\nWhen viewing a &bContraption&r, 3 Screens will show up. The Contraption Diagram, Force chart, and Propulsion chart. \\n\\nWe can press K to Edit the screens like moving them out of the middle of your screen, or changing their size so you can see some part of what you're looking at, or just disabling their visibility. \\n\\nYou can also press J to interact with the Contraption Diagram like zooming in or checking the Forces there. \\n\\n(These can also go in Curios unlike Avaitor's Goggles!)"]
	quest.5D4FED39B07424E4.quest_desc: ["This Quest has been authored by &6AllTheMods Staff&r, or a &2Community contributor&r for use in AllTheMods Modpacks.\\n\\nAs all &6AllTheMods&r packs are licensed under &eAll Rights Reserved&r, this Quest is not allowed to be used in any public packs not released by &6AllTheMods Team&r without explicit permission.\\n\\nThis quest is intentionally hidden, if you're seeing this, you're in editing mode."]
	quest.5D4FED39B07424E4.quest_subtitle: ""
	quest.5D4FED39B07424E4.title: ""
	quest.600D34AC19DA23D9.quest_desc: ["&ePedals&r work like &eLevers&r, they take an Input to go forwards or an Input to go backwards. \\n\\nOnce you let go of the &ePedal's&r input though, it will return back to 0. Unlike the &eLever&r which will stay where it is put. \\n\\nThey are also unique in where they're placed. &ePedals&r get placed on the bottom of the &cControl Desk/Stand&r. Here you can place 3 of them."]
	quest.600D34AC19DA23D9.title: "&ePedal Module"
	quest.665D83912C2A21B1.quest_desc: ["Our &bThrusters&r aren't only used for generating &bThrust&r. \\n\\nWell they are... unless you toss in one of these &9Upgrades&r into them! \\n\\nEach of these &9Upgrades&r will change the &bThruster&r basically into an &6Encased Fan&r. Use Smelting and it will Smelt Items, use Smoking and it will Smoke Food, and Haunting will allow it to Haunt Items. \\n\\nThe better the &9Upgrade&r the more range and efficient the &bThruster&r is."]
	quest.665D83912C2A21B1.title: "Different &bThruster&r Modes"
	quest.68829D24E5DB1DDB.quest_desc: ["&eLever Modules&r go forward and backwards. \\n\\nThey can be placed in the Small Module areas or Large Module areas. \\n\\nEach &eLever&r can be toggled to change their Keybinds and &cFrequencies&r, but their default is W for forward and S for backwards. \\n\\nMoving the &eLever&r forward will go from 0 to 15, this determines the &cRedstone Signal Strength&r sent out. It will keep sending that &cSignal &runtil you move the &eLever&r. \\n\\nIf you move it backwards into the Blue Numbers, it will send a &cRedstone Signal&r of that strength to the other &cFrequency&r. \\n\\nYou can also add &eButton Modules&r on top or on the side of each &eLever&r!"]
	quest.68829D24E5DB1DDB.title: "&eLever Module"
	quest.770DD8ADBDA02586.quest_desc: ["&7Copycat versions&r are the Framed Blocks of &cControl Desks/Stands&r. \\n\\nYou can place any Block you want in the Frames to change its look. \\n\\nPerfect for when the normal one doesn't fit your Build!"]
	quest.770DD8ADBDA02586.title: "&7Copycat Control Desk/Stand"
	quest.7A62568DDA98DAA7.quest_desc: ["The &cJoystick&r combines the &eButton Module&r and &eJoystick Module&r into one &cRedstone Machine&r separate from the need of &cControl Desks/Stands&r. \\n\\nShift Right Clicking will let us toggle the &cFrequencies&r and Functions of the &eButton&r and &eJoystick&r. \\n\\nThen, Right Click it to start using it. Left Click will use the &eButton&r while moving your Mouse will set different &cSignals&r based on where you look. \\n\\nHolding Shift will allow you to look anywhere you want without affecting the &cRedstone Signal&r. And once you're done using the &cJoystick&r just hit ESC to be free."]
	quest.7A62568DDA98DAA7.title: "&cJoystick"
	quest.7C3CE6B746C8D48A.quest_desc: ["&dMechanical Servos&r will take in &dRotational Power&r and a &cRedstone Signal&r to move &dRotational Power&r to a specific angle. \\n\\nThe angle it goes to is determined by the set angle when you Right Click the &dServo&r, and the Strength of the &cRedstone Signal&r given to it. \\n\\nWhen it stops recieving a&c Signal&r it will return the angle to normal. \\n\\nUsing its GUI will also allow us to change the direction it turns."]
	quest.7C3CE6B746C8D48A.title: "&dMechanical Servo"
	task.001544F116F17F7F.title: "Tilt Adapters"
	task.0EE5A9F37B3BCFA9.title: "Vector Thrusters"
	task.1DAB15A2672C0125.title: "Pedal Module"
	task.2C6E6219C652BF6B.title: "Burners"
	task.2E3FA4DCC0696DF5.title: "AllRightsReserved"
	task.34F83DAD52A245A6.title: "Lever Module"
	task.3B190D17076758D8.title: "Button Keypad Module"
	task.427350BF8211E530.title: "AllRightsReserved"
	task.4E019DAF6A6C0D70.title: "Thruster"
	task.5696FDE8E8685EF5.title: "Different Thruster Modes"
	task.570236767095F98D.title: "Control Desk/Stand"
	task.5E242FAF19A3DEB7.title: "Wings"
	task.64A7F1DDA57D52E9.title: "Button Module"
	task.6757180E0CB69A2D.title: "Joystick Module"
	task.6ED5A02083540E31.title: "Button Panel Module"
	task.79D0783FBDD0EAEF.title: "Yoke Module"
